    question: "Part 1: Reading (10 points)\nFill in the gaps with the correct words: (0) education, ( ) technology, ( ) opportunities, ( ) future, ( ) skills, ( ) knowledge.\nIn the modern world, (0) education plays a vital role in shaping the (1)........ of young people. Besides gaining academic (2)........ at school, students also need to develop digital (3)........ and use modern (4)........ wisely so that they can find good job (5)........ after graduation.\n\nPart 2: Grammar (15 points)\nChoose the correct answer (a, b, c, or d):\n1. If students ____ consistently every day, they will pass the BacII exam with flying colors.\n   a. study   b. studied   c. will study   d. had studied\n2. Angkor Wat ____ by millions of tourists from around the world every year.\n   a. visits   b. is visited   c. visited   d. was visiting\n3. She has lived in Phnom Penh ____ 2018.\n   a. for   b. during   c. since   d. from\n4. While I ____ my homework last night, the lights went out.\n   a. did   b. am doing   c. was doing   d. have done\n5. You have never been to Siem Reap, ____?\n   a. haven't you   b. have you   c. do you   d. did you\n\nPart 3: Vocabulary (15 points)\nChoose the correct word (a, b, c, or d):\n1. All medicines should be kept out of ____ of small children.\n   a. hand   b. touch   c. contact   d. reach\n2. Many students want to ____ for evening English classes next month.\n   a. participate   b. enroll   c. enter   d. join in\n3. We should protect our ____ by planting more trees and reducing plastic waste.\n   a. environment   b. pollution   c. population   d. development\n\nPart 4: Writing (10 points)\nWrite an essay of at least 80 words on the topic: “The Benefits of Reading Books for Students”.",
