    question: "ប្រឡងសញ្ញា រប្រមធ្យមសិក្សាទុរិយភូមិ\nសម័យប្រឡង: ០៥ ធ្នូ ២០២២\nវិញ្ញ ា សា: ភាសាអង់គ្លេស\nពិន្ទុ:  ៥០\nរយៈគ្ពល: ៦០នាទី\n(ដកស្រង់ដោយ ដ ៀប គីមឈ័រ)\nប្រធាន្\nRead the text and fill the gaps with the words in the box.\nGap one has been done as an example.\n(0) discipline (1) stricter   ( ) situation\n( ) Punishment ( ) reputation  ( ) behavior\n( ) control  ( ) conduct   ( ) freedom\n( ) respect   ( )progressive\nIn most countries, schools were much (1) stricter twenty-\nfive years ago than they are today. Many parents are not at\nall happy with the present (2).................... because they feel\nthat teachers have lost the ability to (3).................. their\nclasses. Some schools in particular have developed a very\nbad (4).................... for the way in which the students\n(5)................ themselves. They no longer seem to have any\n(6) .................... for the school or the teachers who work in\nit. Some experts feel that the reason for these new patterns\nof (7)................... in schools is the result of (8) ......................\nideas in education. They feel that (9). .................. has\nbecome weak because students have been given too much\n(10)..... to choose how they want to spend their time. It is\nno doubt a good idea that physical (11).................\ntraditional kind of education has vanished in most places.\nBut nowadays in many schools no punishment at all is\npossible.\nPart 2: Grammar (15 points)\nThere are four answers after each statement. Only one\nanswer is correct. Choose the correct a, h, cord. The first\none has been done as an example for you.\nExample: We haven't got....b... money to buy a new car yet.\na. quite  b. too much  b. too many d. enough\n1. Good management....... to the employee.\nwill be finished  b.  are listened  c. listen d. listens\n2. He has got a new friend……..works in the bank.\na. whose b. where c. who d. which\n3. Your mother used to visit you quite often……?\na. didn't she   b. doesn't she c. wouldn't she d. hadn’t\nshe\n4.I…….. on the bus when I dropped my wallet.\na.am getting b. get  c. was getting  d. have  gotten\n5. More roads………….. every year.\na. was built b. had built c. are being built\nd. are building\nPart 3: Vocabulary (15 points)\nThere are four answers after each statement. Only one\nanswer is correct. Choose the correct a, b, c or d. The first\none has been done as an example for you.\nExample: What are you going to buy your\nmother.....for... her birthday.\na. conclude b. during c. for  d. at\n1. What are you going to do when you.................school\n a. conclude  b.  end c. complete d. leave\n 2. All medicines should be kept out of………..of children.\na. hand b. touch c. contact d. reach\n3. I le ……... to get some cards for his birthday, but none\narrived.\na-promised  b. exacted  c. assume\nd. supposed\n4. Is it possible to. ...............now for next terms' evening\nclasses?\n a. participate b. join in  c. enroll d. enter\n5............ inform you that your grandmother died ten\nminutes  ago.\n a. apologies b. sorry c. pity  d. regret\n\nPart 4. Writing (10 points) Write an essay in English at least 80\nwords about “How to reduce road accident in Cambodia?”.",
    answer: "អប្ាកំណែ\nPart 1. Reading (10 points)\n 1. stricter   7. behavior\n 2. situation   8. Progressive\n 3. control   9. discipline\n 4. reputation   10. freedom\n 5.couduct   11. punishment\n 6. respect\nPart 2. Grammar (15 points)\n 1. d (listens)\n 2. c (who)\n3. a (didn’t she)\n4. c (was getting)\n5. c (are being built)\nPart 3. Vocabulary (15 points)\n 1. d (leave)\n2. d (reach)\n 3. b (expected)\n5. c (enroll)\n 3. d (regret)\nIV. Writing (10 points)\n 1. Content\n 2. Grammar\n 3. Spelling\n(Sample essay)\nRoad accidents are one of the major causes of death and injury in many countries.\nThey not only affect the lives of the victims and their families, but also impose a\nhuge social and economic burden on society. Therefore, it is important to find\neffective solutions to reduce road accidents and prevent their negative\nconsequences.\nOne of the main causes of road accidents is human error. This includes driving\nunder the influence of alcoh ol or drugs, speeding, disobeying traffic rules, using\nmobile phones while driving, and driving without proper training or license. To\naddress this problem, drivers should be more disciplined and responsible when\nthey are behind the wheel. They should foll ow the speed limit, wear seat belts,\navoid distractions, and respect other road users. Moreover, they should undergo\nregular medical check-ups and driver education programs to ensure their fitness\nand competence.\nAnother cause of road accidents is poor roa d conditions. This includes potholes,\ncracks, bumps, slippery surfaces, inadequate lighting, and unclear signs. These\nfactors can make driving more difficult and dangerous for drivers and pedestrians\nalike. To improve road conditions, the government should  allocate more funds\nand resources for road maintenance and construction. They should also install\nmore speed cameras, traffic lights, speed bumps, zebra crossings, and other\nsafety features in accident-prone areas.\nA third cause of road accidents is vehicle malfunction. This includes brake failure,\ntire blowout, steering failure, engine failure, and other mechanical problems that\ncan affect the performance and safety of vehicles. To prevent vehicle\nmalfunction, drivers should regularly service their vehicl es and check their tires,\nbrakes, lights, and other parts before driving. They should also use quality fuel\nand oil and avoid overloading or modifying their vehicles.\nIn conclusion, road accidents are a serious issue that needs urgent attention and\naction from all stakeholders. By implementing these solutions, we can reduce\nroad accidents and save lives and resources."
